          "text": "# SV-MATH-001 \u2014 Proof Candidate\n\n## 1. Assumptions and bounded claim boundary\n\nBecause no external GCAT/BCAT specification, transition schema, or existing Lean library for StegVerse was supplied, the proof uses the following explicit formal model.\n\n1. **Geometric boundary preservation** means exact forward preservation:\n   \\[\n   f[\\partial S]=\\partial T.\n   \\]\n2. **Bounded divergence** means a transition\u2019s natural-number divergence measure does not exceed the budget assigned to the selected engine.\n3. **Ontological consistency** is a policy-supplied binary compatibility relation between source and target ontology identifiers.\n4. GCAT and BCAT use the same three checks but may have different divergence budgets.\n5. The ALLOW evaluator accepts exactly after all three checks succeed. It may short-circuit in the order geometry, divergence, ontology.\n6. \u201cJointly complete\u201d means **necessary and sufficient for ALLOW under this evaluator**. It does not claim that the three conditions are independent, uniquely minimal, or complete for an unspecified external implementation.\n7. For categorical composition, ontological consistency is preserved only when the compatibility relation is transitive and the intermediate ontology identifiers agree.\n\nThe definitions and theorems below are generated proof content. They have **not** been compiled or kernel-checked in a Lean 4 environment.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Mathematical definitions\n\nLet a transition\n\\[\nt : \\alpha \\longrightarrow \\beta\n\\]\ncontain:\n\n- source boundary \\(\\partial_s(t)\\subseteq\\alpha\\),\n- target boundary \\(\\partial_t(t)\\subseteq\\beta\\),\n- map \\(f_t:\\alpha\\to\\beta\\),\n- divergence \\(d(t)\\in\\mathbb N\\),\n- source ontology \\(o_s(t)\\),\n- target ontology \\(o_t(t)\\).\n\nFor engine \\(E\\in\\{\\mathrm{GCAT},\\mathrm{BCAT}\\}\\), let \\(B(E)\\) be its divergence budget, and let \\(C(a,b)\\) denote ontology compatibility.\n\nDefine:\n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{Geom}(t)\n\\iff\nf_t[\\partial_s(t)]=\\partial_t(t),\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{Bounded}(E,t)\n\\iff\nd(t)\\le B(E),\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{Ont}(t)\n\\iff\nC(o_s(t),o_t(t)).\n\\]\n\nThe evaluator is:\n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{eval}(E,t)=\n\\begin{cases}\n\\operatorname{denyGeometry}, & \\neg\\operatorname{Geom}(t),\\\\\n\\operatorname{denyDivergence},&\n \\operatorname{Geom}(t)\\land\\neg\\operatorname{Bounded}(E,t),\\\\\n\\operatorname{denyOntology},&\n \\operatorname{Geom}(t)\\land\\operatorname{Bounded}(E,t)\n \\land\\neg\\operatorname{Ont}(t),\\\\\n\\operatorname{allow},&\n \\operatorname{Geom}(t)\\land\\operatorname{Bounded}(E,t)\n \\land\\operatorname{Ont}(t).\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nAdmissibility is defined operationally:\n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{Admissible}(E,t)\n\\iff\n\\operatorname{eval}(E,t)=\\operatorname{allow}.\n\\]\n\n---\n\n## 3. Main theorem\n\n### Theorem SV-MATH-001\n\nFor either GCAT or BCAT and every transition \\(t\\),\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\operatorname{Admissible}(E,t)\n\\iff\n\\operatorname{Geom}(t)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{Bounded}(E,t)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{Ont}(t)\n}\n\\]\n\nTherefore geometric boundary preservation, bounded divergence, and ontological consistency are jointly necessary and sufficient\u2014and hence jointly complete\u2014for ALLOW admissibility under the stated evaluator.\n\n### Proof reasoning\n\n- **Necessity:** If the evaluator returns ALLOW, it cannot have taken any denial branch. Therefore geometry succeeded, divergence was within the selected engine\u2019s budget, and ontology compatibility succeeded.\n- **Sufficiency:** If all three predicates hold, each denial condition is false. Evaluation reaches the final ALLOW branch.\n- These directions establish the biconditional.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Lean 4 proof candidate\n\n```lean\nimport Mathlib\n\nnamespace StegVerse\n\nuniverse u v w\n\n/-- The two modeled engine families. -/\ninductive EngineKind\n  | GCAT\n  | BCAT\n  deriving DecidableEq, Repr\n\n/--\nA policy supplies engine-specific divergence budgets and an\nontology-compatibility relation.\n-/\nstructure EnginePolicy where\n  gcatBudget : Nat\n  bcatBudget : Nat\n  compatible : Nat \u2192 Nat \u2192 Prop\n\n/-- Select the divergence budget associated with an engine. -/\ndef EnginePolicy.budget\n    (p : EnginePolicy) (engine : EngineKind) : Nat :=\n  match engine with\n  | .GCAT => p.gcatBudget\n  | .BCAT => p.bcatBudget\n\n/--\nA transition between carrier types `\u03b1` and `\u03b2`.\n\nBoundary sets model the geometric boundary data. Ontology identifiers\nare represented by natural numbers; a production implementation may\nreplace them with a dedicated ontology type.\n-/\nstructure Transition (\u03b1 : Type u) (\u03b2 : Type v) where\n  srcBoundary : Set \u03b1\n  dstBoundary : Set \u03b2\n  map : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2\n  divergence : Nat\n  srcOntology : Nat\n  dstOntology : Nat\n\n/--\nExact forward geometric boundary preservation:\nthe image of the source boundary equals the target boundary.\n-/\ndef GeometricBoundaryPreservation\n    (t : Transition \u03b1 \u03b2) : Prop :=\n  t.map '' t.srcBoundary = t.dstBoundary\n\n/-- The transition divergence is within the selected engine budget. -/\ndef BoundedDivergence\n    (p : EnginePolicy)\n    (engine : EngineKind)\n    (t : Transition \u03b1 \u03b2) : Prop :=\n  t.divergence \u2264 p.budget engine\n\n/-- Source and target ontology identifiers are policy-compatible. -/\ndef OntologicalConsistency\n    (p : EnginePolicy)\n    (t : Transition \u03b1 \u03b2) : Prop :=\n  p.compatible t.srcOntology t.dstOntology\n\n/-- Observable outcomes of the modeled ALLOW gate. -/\ninductive GateDecision\n  | allow\n  | denyGeometry\n  | denyDivergence\n  | denyOntology\n  deriving DecidableEq, Repr\n\n/--\nGCAT/BCAT ALLOW-gate evaluation.\n\nThe checks short-circuit in the order:\n1. geometric boundary preservation,\n2. bounded divergence,\n3. ontological consistency.\n-/\nnoncomputable def evaluate\n    (p : EnginePolicy)\n    (engine : EngineKind)\n    (t : Transition \u03b1 \u03b2) : GateDecision := by\n  classical\n  exact\n    if GeometricBoundaryPreservation t then\n      if BoundedDivergence p engine t then\n        if OntologicalConsistency p t then\n          .allow\n        else\n          .denyOntology\n      else\n        .denyDivergence\n    else\n      .denyGeometry\n\n/-- Operational ALLOW admissibility. -/\ndef Admissible\n    (p : EnginePolicy)\n    (engine : EngineKind)\n    (t : Transition \u03b1 \u03b2) : Prop :=\n  evaluate p engine t = .allow\n\n/--\nSV-MATH-001.\n\nThe three gate conditions are jointly necessary and sufficient\nfor ALLOW admissibility.\n-/\ntheorem allow_iff_conditions\n    (p : EnginePolicy)\n    (engine : EngineKind)\n    (t : Transition \u03b1 \u03b2) :\n    Admissible p engine t \u2194\n      GeometricBoundaryPreservation t \u2227\n      BoundedDivergence p engine t \u2227\n      OntologicalConsistency p t := by\n  classical\n  simp [Admissible"
